-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Mixed Scalar Close Left Front Scalar
-- statement:
--   **The mixed switcheroo scalar is within the self-consistency square root of the left-front scalar.**
--
--   Let `psi_bi` be normalized, let `family` and `M` be as specified, and assume complete G self consistency at level `zeta`. If $S_{\mathrm{mix}}$ is the mixed aggregate scalar and $S_{\mathrm{front}}$ is the left-front aggregate scalar, then
--
--   $$
--   \left|S_{\mathrm{mix}}-S_{\mathrm{front}}\right|\le\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   The estimate is the fourth-term-chain comparison that replaces the mixed expression by the left-front expression. Normalization supplies the state bounds, while complete self consistency controls the difference.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateMixedScalar_close_leftFrontScalar`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
